Sval: Remote Settings does not report requests the shutdown refused as errors

Quitting within seconds of a fresh profile's first start refuses Remote
Settings' first downloads with NS_ERROR_ILLEGAL_DURING_SHUTDOWN, and the
call sites that log each refusal with console.error log at debug while the
app shuts down. Mozilla already treats shutdown as expected here (sync()
warns "sync interrupted by shutdown" and reports SHUTDOWN_ERROR).

